#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jav3-desk — lets a Jav3 server see and drive this computer, when allowed.

    jav3-desk login          paste the line from Settings → Add computer
    jav3-desk run            connect and serve (what the service runs)
    jav3-desk install        write a systemd --user unit / launchd agent
    jav3-desk uninstall      remove it
    jav3-desk allow-shell    let the server run shell commands here (asks first
    jav3-desk deny-shell       in Settings unless allowlisted); off by default
    jav3-desk panic          stop everything now; needs `resume` to come back
    jav3-desk resume
    jav3-desk status

It dials OUT (one WebSocket to <server>/api/desk/ws) and waits for requests.
Nothing listens on this machine. What the server may do is decided twice:
Settings → Computer use on the server (screen / input / shell), and the local
ceiling here, which the server cannot lift — shell stays off until someone at
this keyboard runs `jav3-desk allow-shell`.

Every request is a verb from a closed list with typed, bounded parameters,
re-validated here (ACTIONS / validate). Every program is run with an argv list
and shell=False, from a binary resolved once at startup — except `shell`, the
one deliberate exception, which needs the local flag AND the server's grant.

Backends (auto-detected, or --backend):
  hyprland  grim (JPEG) · wtype · hyprctl + wlroots virtual pointer
  sway      grim · wtype · wlroots virtual pointer
  x11       import/maim/scrot · xdotool (also the headless test backend, Xvfb)
  macos     screencapture + sips · Quartz (ctypes) · needs the Accessibility
            and Screen Recording grants (see `jav3-desk status`)
  uinput    TODO(M2): stub — /dev/uinput for GNOME/KDE Wayland

Every screenshot carries a numbered element list from the accessibility tree
(docs/navigation-contract.md A.2), boxes in pixels of the returned image:
macOS AXUIElement (ctypes; needs Accessibility), X11 AT-SPI2 (gi Atspi, else
python3-dbus). Wayland backends and Windows send none, with the reason.
`region` zooms a screenshot; every input verb waits for the screen to settle
and says whether it changed (A.4); `wait` and `drag` are verbs too (A.3).

A locked screen or a sleeping display is reported, not fought: the hello and
a `state {locked, asleep}` frame (sent when it changes, polled every
STATE_POLL_S) carry it, and screenshot / wait / input verbs are refused with
one sentence asking the operator to unlock or wake it (macOS: CGSession +
CGDisplayIsAsleep; Linux: logind LockedHint, then the ScreenSaver D-Bus; unknown = null).

Files, in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jav3 (default ~/.config/jav3), dir 0700:
  desk.json          {"address", "token"} 0600
  desk-shell         present = shell allowed at this computer
  desk.paused        present = panic; `resume` removes it
  desk-apps.json     optional {"name": ["argv", ...]} for desk_open app=
Needs Python 3.11+ and websockets; nothing else.
"""
